<section class="hero"><div class="wrap hero-split">
<h1>Two students, one clinic, a hundred mothers at a time.</h1>
<div>
<p class="lead">Heartlines International was founded in 2026 by Jason Ham and Allison Kim, high school students in San Jose, California, to bring practical health support and real encouragement to mothers who are often overlooked.</p>
</div>
</div></section>

<section><div class="wrap split">
<div>
<h2>Our story</h2>
<p class="prose">It began with a mission trip to the Philippines in February 2026, where co-founders Jason Ham and Allison Kim saw firsthand the work of a free maternity clinic that cares for about 450&ndash;500 mothers a year, many of them young and on their own. Iron-deficiency anaemia is common and serious in pregnancy,<a class="ref" href="#src1" aria-label="Source 1">[1]</a> yet mothers often skip medication they don't see as essential, and the emotional weight of new motherhood too often goes unaddressed.<a class="ref" href="#src5" aria-label="Source 5">[5]</a></p>
<p class="prose">Together they set out to build something that lasts: health guides in Tagalog and English, checked by the clinic's medical team, handwritten encouragement from student volunteers, and iron tablets the clinic buys locally, delivered cycle after cycle.</p>
</div>
<aside class="approach" aria-label="Our approach"><h3>Clinic-led, not guesswork.</h3><p>The clinic tells us what its mothers need. Its medical team checks every guide before we print, and its licensed staff buy and give the iron locally.</p></aside>
</div></section>

